    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0568" n="554" xml:id="pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.W./9–2144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Alexander C. Kirk, United States Political Adviser
                        on the Staff of the Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-21T00:00:00+01:00">September 21,
                            1944—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received September 22—8:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>484. My 324, September 7, midnight, second paragraph. On instructions from SACMED
                    member of Maclean’s Mission recently interviewed Tito<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d322-f1"/> with view to obtaining latter’s agreement to application
                    of principles governing surrender of Germans recently enunciated by CCS. Tito
                    fully agreed and is issuing instructions to his corps commanders accordingly. It
                    is reported that he proposes to place Germans surrendering in concentration
                    camps for road work in Yugoslavia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d322-f1" n="16" xml:id="d322-f1-content">
                <p>Marshal Josip Broz-Tito, Commander of the Yugoslav National Army of Liberation,
                    and President of the National Committee of Liberation of Yugoslavia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
